{"id": "arc_challenge/test/939", "source": "arc_challenge", "primitive": "choice", "split": "test", "state": "{\"question\": \"Black fur is dominant to white fur in guinea pigs. If two black guinea pigs (Bb) are crossed, what color will the fur of their offspring be?\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"choice\", \"instructions\": \"Which option is the correct answer to `question`?\", \"criteria\": {\"A\": \"100% black\", \"B\": \"100% white\", \"C\": \"50% black, 50% white\", \"D\": \"75% black, 25% white\"}}", "label": "D", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"allenai/ai2_arc\", \"license\": \"cc-by-sa-4.0\", \"domain\": \"knowledge\", \"task_family\": \"mcq\", \"hf_config\": \"ARC-Challenge\", \"arc_id\": \"Mercury_402364\"}"}
{"id": "arc_challenge/test/162", "source": "arc_challenge", "primitive": "choice", "split": "test", "state": "{\"question\": \"A lake that received runoff from surrounding farmland had a healthy fish population. Several years ago, a new type of pesticide was used to treat crops. As runoff entered the lake, it killed an insect that was a primary food source for fish. Which will most likely occur if farmers in the area stop using the pesticide?\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"choice\", \"instructions\": \"Which option is the correct answer to `question`?\", \"criteria\": {\"A\": \"The population of fish will increase.\", \"B\": \"The insects will become more resistant to the pesticide.\", \"C\": \"The lake will be unable to support life.\", \"D\": \"The fish will find another food source.\"}}", "label": "A", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"allenai/ai2_arc\", \"license\": \"cc-by-sa-4.0\", \"domain\": \"knowledge\", \"task_family\": \"mcq\", \"hf_config\": \"ARC-Challenge\", \"arc_id\": \"Mercury_7142415\"}"}
{"id": "arc_challenge/test/462", "source": "arc_challenge", "primitive": "choice", "split": "test", "state": "{\"question\": \"Early Egyptians thought the solar system was a rectangular box. People in early Greece pictured the universe as a set of crystal-like spheres. Later the solar system was viewed as a set of planets orbiting the Sun. Why has the model of the solar system changed over the centuries?\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"choice\", \"instructions\": \"Which option is the correct answer to `question`?\", \"criteria\": {\"A\": \"Scientists preferred newer models.\", \"B\": \"New evidence caused revisions.\", \"C\": \"The newer models were easier to draw.\", \"D\": \"The information was finally put in books.\"}}", "label": "B", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"allenai/ai2_arc\", \"license\": \"cc-by-sa-4.0\", \"domain\": \"knowledge\", \"task_family\": \"mcq\", \"hf_config\": \"ARC-Challenge\", \"arc_id\": \"Mercury_7205870\"}"}
{"id": "arc_challenge/test/940", "source": "arc_challenge", "primitive": "choice", "split": "test", "state": "{\"question\": \"The nucleus of the cell controls cell activity. Which body system performs a similar function in humans?\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"choice\", \"instructions\": \"Which option is the correct answer to `question`?\", \"criteria\": {\"A\": \"circulatory system\", \"B\": \"central nervous system\", \"C\": \"skeletal system\", \"D\": \"integumentary system\"}}", "label": "B", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"allenai/ai2_arc\", \"license\": \"cc-by-sa-4.0\", \"domain\": \"knowledge\", \"task_family\": \"mcq\", \"hf_config\": \"ARC-Challenge\", \"arc_id\": \"Mercury_7263183\"}"}
{"id": "arc_challenge/test/482", "source": "arc_challenge", "primitive": "choice", "split": "test", "state": "{\"question\": \"A student has built a model in which sheets of cork floating in a tub of water represent tectonic plates. To make the sheet representing an ocean plate more accurate in the model system, the student should\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"choice\", \"instructions\": \"Which option is the correct answer to `question`?\", \"criteria\": {\"A\": \"cut several holes in it.\", \"B\": \"attach small weights to it.\", \"C\": \"cut it into a smaller shape.\", \"D\": \"replace it with a thin sheet of copper.\"}}", "label": "B", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"allenai/ai2_arc\", \"license\": \"cc-by-sa-4.0\", \"domain\": \"knowledge\", \"task_family\": \"mcq\", \"hf_config\": \"ARC-Challenge\", \"arc_id\": \"Mercury_7027720\"}"}
{"id": "arc_challenge/test/1019", "source": "arc_challenge", "primitive": "choice", "split": "test", "state": "{\"question\": \"Some students wanted to make a model to show how the size of the moon compares with the size of Earth. They used an orange to represent the moon. Which of the following would best represent Earth?\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"choice\", \"instructions\": \"Which option is the correct answer to `question`?\", \"criteria\": {\"A\": \"A cantaloupe\", \"B\": \"A grape\", \"C\": \"A lime\", \"D\": \"A cherry\"}}", "label": "A", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"allenai/ai2_arc\", \"license\": \"cc-by-sa-4.0\", \"domain\": \"knowledge\", \"task_family\": \"mcq\", \"hf_config\": \"ARC-Challenge\", \"arc_id\": \"TAKS_2009_5_30\"}"}
{"id": "arc_challenge/test/351", "source": "arc_challenge", "primitive": "choice", "split": "test", "state": "{\"question\": \"Robert is thinking about buying a new refrigerator. His old refrigerator runs at about 43% efficiency. Which most likely accounts for the remaining 57% of the energy?\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"choice\", \"instructions\": \"Which option is the correct answer to `question`?\", \"criteria\": {\"A\": \"It is used up by the light in the refrigerator.\", \"B\": \"It is released to the surroundings as heat.\", \"C\": \"It is converted into mechanical energy.\", \"D\": \"It stored as a form of potential energy.\"}}", "label": "B", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"allenai/ai2_arc\", \"license\": \"cc-by-sa-4.0\", \"domain\": \"knowledge\", \"task_family\": \"mcq\", \"hf_config\": \"ARC-Challenge\", \"arc_id\": \"Mercury_409295\"}"}
{"id": "arc_challenge/test/1075", "source": "arc_challenge", "primitive": "choice", "split": "test", "state": "{\"question\": \"Some space telescopes search for extrasolar planets. The ability to observe which phenomenon is most important for these telescopes' purpose?\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"choice\", \"instructions\": \"Which option is the correct answer to `question`?\", \"criteria\": {\"A\": \"fluctuations in the size of a star\", \"B\": \"wobbles in the position of a star\", \"C\": \"flickers in the brightness of a star\", \"D\": \"changes in the fuel source of a star\"}}", "label": "C", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"allenai/ai2_arc\", \"license\": \"cc-by-sa-4.0\", \"domain\": \"knowledge\", \"task_family\": \"mcq\", \"hf_config\": \"ARC-Challenge\", \"arc_id\": \"Mercury_7233398\"}"}
